# CKA Drill: Manual Kubeadm Cluster Upgrade (`upgrade`)

Hands-on rehearsal of the manual Kubernetes node and cluster upgrade sequence using `kubeadm`, `kubelet`, and `kubectl`.

## Exam Importance & Constraints

- **Exam Domain**: Cluster Architecture, Installation & Configuration (25%).
- **Frequency**: Present in nearly every CKA exam session.
- **Rules of Thumb**:
  - Always upgrade the control plane node before any worker nodes.
  - Never skip minor versions (e.g. 1.33 $\to$ 1.34 $\to$ 1.35; never 1.33 $\to$ 1.35 directly).
  - Version skew: `kubelet` must never be newer than `kube-apiserver`, and can be at most 1 minor version older.
  - Always `drain` before upgrading `kubelet` on worker nodes; unhold packages before running `apt-get install`.

